  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 319 AM MST FRI NOV 20 2026\nLight valley rain and mountain snow will continue through \nMonday morning, with minimal accumulations anticipated. A ridge \nof high pressure will build back into the region by late Monday,\nbringing a short-lived warming and drying trend. A deep upper \nlevel low and associated atmospheric river will begin to move \ntowards the PacNW coast on Wednesday, eventually splitting and \nstaying offshore. Remnant moisture from this system will be \nadvected into the region thanks to southwest flow aloft, \nbringing more valley rain and mountain snow by midweek. \nPrecipitation will mainly be in southeast Oregon and over higher\nterrain in southwest Idaho. Model agreement diverges \nsignificantly after Thursday, primarily on the position of an \nupper level low just west of Vancouver Island and the strength \nof a ridge of high pressure over the West Coast. The current \nlong term forecast favors the warmer and drier scenario, which \nwould keep the ridge of high pressure stronger and over the \nIntermountain West.",
